--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.unary.op]/3.1, [conv.mem]/2: &D::in has type
int (B::*)(int) const because in is a member of B; it converts to
int (D::*)(int) const.  Initializing a pointer to member function from the
address of a function took the class of the target type and required the
types to be identical ("conversion from 'signed int (const struct D::
*)(const struct B *, signed int)' to ...", bin53).  libstdc++'s
__str_codecvt_in initializes `_ConvFn __fn = &codecvt<_CharT, char,
_State>::in;' with in a member of __codecvt_abstract_base, so its body was
dropped (cpp17_filesystem_basic once path::generic_string's body was
attached).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++98), and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
